ention—reported in approximately one-third of patients. Separately, concurrent use with 地戈辛 (digoxin) can lead to severe bradycardia. These findings highlight the drug's potential to affect both central nervous system function and cardiac rhythm, necessitating vigilant monitoring during therapy [Data: Relationships (14174, 14173); Entities (16126, 6965)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"High-protein foods and diets modulate anticoagulant and bronchodilator efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"高蛋白食物 and 高蛋白饮食 are linked to altered pharmacokinetics of several medications, most notably 华法林. Evidence shows that high-protein diets reduce the anticoagulant effect of 华法林, potentially increasing thrombotic risk in patients reliant on stable INR control. Additionally, such diets increase the hepatic clearance of 茶碱 (theophylline), which could diminish its bronchodilator efficacy in asthma or COPD patients. These diet-drug interactions emphasize the importance of dietary consistency and counseling for patients on narrow-therapeutic-index drugs [Data: Relationships (31145, 31146); Entities (12947, 12948)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"呱乙啶 enhances 甲基多巴’s antihypertensive effect but poses interaction risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"呱乙啶 is documented to potentiate the blood pressure-lowering effect of 甲基多巴, suggesting a synergistic pharmacodynamic interaction useful in resistant hypertension. However, 呱乙啶 itself has complex interactions—it can amplify the pressor effects of sympathomimetics like 去甲肾上腺素, leading to severe and sustained hypertension. While not directly causing adverse effects with 甲基多巴 beyond enhanced hypotension, its inclusion in a polypharmacy regimen increases overall interaction complexity and requires cautious dose titration [Data: Relationships (44652); Entities (4459, 6965)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"多种维生素/矿物质 may reduce 甲基多巴 bioavailability\",\n            \"explanatio